        "finish_reason": "stop",
        "complete_raw_answer": "The unfolded paper shows 4 holes arranged in a rectangular pattern: Top-Left (red), Top-Right (blue), Bottom-Left (blue), and Bottom-Right (red).\n\nThis pattern of holes is symmetric about the horizontal line passing through the center of the square.\n\nLet's test the fold lines:\n*   **Folding along a vertical line (like in Choice E):** A fold along the vertical centerline would create vertical pairs of holes (Left holes mirroring Right holes). The colors would match (e.g., Top-Left mirrors Top-Right). Since Top-Left is Red and Top-Right is Blue, a vertical fold is not possible.\n*   **Folding along a diagonal line (like in Choice A):** A diagonal fold would create pairs along the diagonal. For example, folding along the top-right to bottom-left diagonal ($y = -x$) would swap the Top-Left (Red) and Bottom-Right (Red) positions. This is consistent with them being the same color. Similarly, it swaps Top-Right (Blue) and Bottom-Left (Blue). This fits the color pattern perfectly. A diagonal fold creates the characteristic alternating color pattern.\n\nTherefore, the fold must be diagonal.\n\nAnswer: A",
